course: dictionary
lesson: 14839
title: RAF: a short word for a big air force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: RAF is an abbreviation, a short form of longer words. It stands for the Royal Air Force, the air force of the United Kingdom. «My cousin wants to become a pilot in the RAF.» The words pilot and air force are the clues: a pilot flies planes, so the RAF must be a force of planes and flyers.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. When you see RAF written in capitals, think of the full name. «The RAF base is near the coast, so the planes can take off over the sea.» Base means the place where the air force keeps its planes and people.
explain: Other countries have similar names. RAAF, RNZAF and RCAF are the Royal Australian, New Zealand and Canadian Air Forces. «The RAAF jets flew over Sydney Harbour.» Each short form follows the same pattern: the first letter of each important word, with the country first.
explain: Context can also show you a special meaning. «The Red Arrows, the RAF display team, flew in a heart shape over the beach.» A display team flies to entertain crowds at air shows, so you can work out that the RAF is an air force that performs in the sky too.
fact: RAF stands for Royal Air Force.
fact: The RAF is the air force of the United Kingdom and was founded in 1918.
fact: In 1940 the RAF fought in the Battle of Britain, a famous battle in the air.
fact: RAAF, RNZAF and RCAF stand for the Royal Australian, New Zealand and Canadian Air Forces.
fact: Abbreviations are short forms of longer words, and they are often written in capital letters.
exercise: «She wants to fly jets when she joins the RAF.» What does RAF stand for? | *Royal Air Force | Royal Air Fleet | Really Amazing Flyers | Royal Army Force
exercise: The RAF is the air force of which country? | *The United Kingdom | New Zealand | Canada | Australia
exercise: What does RCAF stand for? | Royal Australian Air Force | Royal Chinese Air Force | Royal Cardiff Air Force | *Royal Canadian Air Force
test: «The Red Arrows, the RAF display team, flew over the beach.» What kind of team is the Red Arrows? | *A display team that flies at air shows | A team of divers | A rescue team at sea | Football team
test: The RAF fought in which famous battle in 1940? | *Battle of Britain | Battle of Waterloo | Battle of Hastings | Battle of the Somme
exam: Which statement about the RAF is correct? | *RAF stands for Royal Air Force and is the air force of the United Kingdom | RAF is a type of aeroplane | RAF means Royal Army Force | The RAF is the navy of the United Kingdom
